-- R1 of specs/todo/PATTERN-REFERENCE-RULE-SPEC.md: the selector carve-out is
-- an ARGUMENT-position rule, and this is the file that pins it.
--
-- `amount` is a field of the action's own `pay` constructor and nothing else.
-- In an ARGUMENT slot that spelling names the slot being filled and is a
-- deliberate placeholder (see ok/regulative-reference-selector-wildcard.l4).
-- At the HEAD there is no slot to name: the whole action is being written, and
-- a field of an action is not an action. So the name refers, and fails the
-- rule's declared type -- which is what this file shows, and what the head
-- rule has done since 34a7c1c5.
--
-- Carving selectors out here as well would make `amount` a fresh name at the
-- head, and a fresh name at the head matches EVERY action: the obligation
-- would be discharged by `ship 3`. The review of 2026-09-16 found exactly
-- that, which is why this fixture exists.

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    Buyer

DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
    pay  HAS amount IS A NUMBER
    ship HAS count  IS A NUMBER

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`head names a field` MEANS
    PARTY Buyer MUST amount WITHIN 30 HENCE FULFILLED LEST BREACH
